course: dictionary
lesson: 12191
title: Words for a happy scene
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture before you even see the scene. Read the words around an unknown word to find its meaning. «The crowd cheered as the bride walked out, and the air filled with confetti.» Cheered and bride tell you this is a celebration, so confetti must be something thrown into the air for fun.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Lena swept the bright bits off the floor after the party.» Try "Lena swept the tiny coloured pieces off the floor after the party." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Confetti is an uncountable noun, so we say some confetti, not two confettis. You can talk about one tiny piece as a piece of confetti. Writers use confetti to show a happy, noisy scene.
fact: Confetti means tiny pieces of coloured paper thrown into the air at weddings, parties and parades.
fact: Confetti can also mean anything lying about in many tiny bright bits, like «a confetti of petals».
fact: Some confetti is made of small sugar sweets or sprinkles that decorate cakes.
fact: Confetti is an uncountable noun: you say some confetti, not two confettis.
fact: Many places now use paper or dried-petal confetti, because plastic or glitter confetti can harm nature.
exercise: «The wedding guests threw confetti as the couple walked out.» What is confetti here? | A loud drum played in a parade | *Tiny pieces of coloured paper thrown into the air | A long ribbon tied to the car | A big bunch of flowers
exercise: «The park path was covered in confetti of red and yellow leaves.» What does confetti mean here? | A sudden storm of wind | Sticky sweets dropped on the path | Rain falling on the grass | *Many tiny bright bits lying about
exercise: Mum says, «Sprinkle the confetti on the cake.» What is the confetti here? | Fresh cream | *Small sugar sweets or sprinkles | Icing that has gone hard | A birthday candle
test: «After the parade, the street was covered in confetti everywhere.» What does «confetti everywhere» suggest about the scene? | Empty and dull | Cold and wet | *Happy and noisy | Quiet and sad
test: Ravi says, «I have three confettis.» Which is the correct way to say it? | Two confettis | *Some confetti | Ten confettis | Three confettis
exam: The class made a collage with paper confetti, because the teacher said glitter is bad for nature. Why do many places now use paper confetti instead of glitter? | Paper sparkles more than glitter | It is cheaper to buy glitter | *Plastic and glitter confetti can harm nature | Glitter is much heavier to carry
